# Hon-SMA uptime check + Supabase keep-alive.
# Install on the VPS (the box that already runs hon-sma-worker under pm2):
#   crontab -l 2>/dev/null | cat - scripts/healthcheck.cron | crontab -
#
# Every 10 minutes. That is far more often than the ~7-day Supabase idle-pause
# threshold, so the project can never fall asleep again, and it catches an
# outage within 10 minutes instead of never.
#
# Set ALERT_WEBHOOK to get told when something breaks. ntfy.sh needs no signup:
# pick a long random topic name, subscribe in the ntfy phone app, then use
#   ALERT_WEBHOOK=https://ntfy.sh/<your-random-topic>
# Leave it unset and the check still runs and still logs, it just stays quiet.
# INSTALLED AND VERIFIED ON THE VPS 2026-09-22. Two things the obvious line got
# wrong, both found by running it under a stripped cron environment:
#  1. node is installed under nvm, which is NOT on cron's minimal PATH, so a bare
#     `/usr/bin/env node` died with "node: command not found". Hence the PATH prefix.
#  2. /var/log is not writable by devjoy and there is no passwordless sudo, so the
#     log lives in the home directory instead.
# Node path is pinned to the installed version. An nvm upgrade WILL break this line.
*/10 * * * * cd /home/devjoy/Hon-SMA && set -a && . ./.env && set +a && PATH=/home/devjoy/.nvm/versions/node/v24.18.0/bin:$PATH /usr/bin/env node scripts/healthcheck.mjs >> /home/devjoy/hon-sma-health.log 2>&1
